  <data name="lblSearchingInfo.Text" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>To search for appointments servicing a specific vehicle or serviced by a specific mechanic, you may select these using the provided comboboxes. Upon clicking the "Search" button, all appointments on the system will be searched against the criteria, and a messagebox with the appropriate appointments - alongside their details - will be displayed</value>
  </data>
  <data name="lblUpdatingInfo.Text" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Appointments are displayed in the provided timetable, with a row for each mechanic, for the selected date. From here, appointments can be selected by clicking the blocks representing them, which will populate the fields on the form with their details. However, do note that only lead mechanics are permitted to view and edit their colleagues' appointments.

Once an appointment is selected, the mechanic servicing the vehicle and the vehicle to be serviced may be selected from the provided comboboxes. Services can be selected by double-clicking the appropriate item in the checked list, which will automatically update the time taken and cost of the appointment. Once a service has been added, parts can be added to it by selecting the appropriate item in the combobox, with quantities editable with the "Plus" and "Minus" buttons. The times of an appointment can be adjusted by dragging and dropping the start or end of a block.

To add a new appointment, the "Insert mode" may be used, where the viewing of existing records will be prohibited, but new appointment blocks can be added by selecting a permitted slot in the timetable. Once a temporary block has been created, its details can be populated as usual.

Once you are happy with your changes, you may use the "Save" button to edit all the details of the currently selected appointment, "Save New Schedule" button to edit the times of all the appointments in the timetables but not their details, or "Add" button to create a new appointment with the provided information. The record may be removed from the system using the "Delete" button.</value>
